MKDIR(1)                    General Commands Manual                   MKDIR(1)

NNAAMMEE
       mkdir - make directories

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       mkdir [ -p ] ddiirreeccttoorryy__nnaammee ...

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       Mkdir creates the directories named as operands, in the order
       specified, using mode 0777 modified by the current umask(2).  On a
       mounted ProDOS volume only the owner's read and write bits reach the
       new directory's access byte; see mount_prodos(8).

       The options are as follows:

       -p     Create intermediate directories as required.  If this option is
              not specified, the full path prefix of each operand must already
              exist.

       Mkdir exits 0 if successful, and >0 if an error occurred.

SSTTAANNDDAARRDDSS
       Mkdir is POSIX 1003.2 compliant.  This manual page is derived from the
       POSIX 1003.2 manual page.

3rd Berkeley Distribution       August 16, 1993                       MKDIR(1)
